# Line endings, pinned for every platform and every autocrlf setting. Without
# this, a clone on Windows checks the committed SVG and CSV out with CRLF while
# the build writes LF, so `python verify.py` compares a file against a variant
# of itself and the acceptance checks disagree with the tree they just passed
# on. Same defect as the one recorded as E75 in Pkkls/autonomy-log, found there
# by rebuilding a release archive and comparing it byte by byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Committed build output. These are the deliverable, so a diff on them should
# be readable rather than a wall of "binary files differ".
*.svg text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
